 Jul 26-29\, with end-of-day AoE deadlines for the 8-page abstract (Feb 1)
 \, full paper (Feb 4) and 2-page extended abstract (Apr 1). Event proposa
 ls (GACs\, community events) are due Mar 18\; a fuller dates page is pend
 ing.\nScope: Cognitive computational neuroscience\, connecting experiment
 s and models of brain computation with artificial intelligence. Character
 istic work compares biological and artificial representations\, models pe
